$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure B: Coupling of Aryl Bromides
with Phenols: A sealed tube equipped with a Teflon valve was charged with
a magnetic stir bar, CuBr (14 mg, 0.10mmol, 10 mol %), Cs2CO3 (650 mg, 2
mmol) and any remaining solids (phenols and/or aryl halides). The tube
was evacuated and backfilled with argon (this procedure was repeated
three times). Under a counter flow of argon, 1.2 mmol phenols (if
liquid), 1 mmol aryl halide (if liquid), DMSO (1.5 mL) and ligand L1 (27
mg, 0.2 mmol, 20 mol %) were added by syringe. The tube was evacuated and
backfilled with argon again (this procedure was repeated three times) and
sealed. The reaction mixture was heated to the indicated temperature
(90℃) for the required time period. After cooling to room temperature,
the mixture was diluted with ethyl acetate (10 ml), passed through a
fritted glass filter to remove the inorganic salts and the solvent was
removed under vacuum. The residue was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel and the product was dried under high vacuum for at least 1
h. 1-methoxy-4-(4-nitrophenoxy) benzeneProcedure B was followed. Yellow
solid: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.17 (2 H, d, J =9.2 Hz), 7.01-7.04 (2
H, m）,6.94-6.98 (4 H, m), 3.84 (3 H, s); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
164.2, 157.2, 147.8, 142.3, 126.0, 121.9, 116.4, 115.3, 55.7 (CDCl3 δ
77.1). GC/MS: rt = 9.60 min, M/Z = 245.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation gave lower yield, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM (2-Pyridyl)acetone-Promoted Cu-Catalyzed O-Arylation of Phenols with Aryl
Iodides, Bromides, and Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhang, Qi; Wang, Deping; Wang, Xianyang; Ding, Ke
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(18), 7187-7190

