$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3-Chloro-4-phenoxyaniline (4a). To a mixture
of 2-chloro-1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (1, 1.75 g, 10.0 mmol) and potassium
carbonate (2.07 g, 10.0 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF) (20 mL) was
added phenol (2a, 941 mg, 10.0 mmol). After being stirred at 80 °C for 2
h, water (40 mL) was added to the mixture and the mixture was extracted
with ethyl acetate (EtOAc). The organic layer was washed with saturated
brine (30 mL), dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate (MgSO4), and
concentrated in vacuo to give 3a (2.32 g) as brown oil. To a solution of
3a (2.32 g, 9.31 mmol) in EtOAc (50 mL) was added 5% platinum-carbon
(Pt-C) (200 mg), and the mixture was stirred under hydrogen atmosphere at
room temperature for 2 h. After 5% Pt-C was filtered off, the filtrate
was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (eluent, EtOAc:hexane = 1:9 to 5:5).
3-Chloro-4-(2-chlorophenoxy)aniline (4d). Yield 97%, brown oil. 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 3.69 (br s, 2H), 6.56 (dd, 1H, J = 8.7, 2.8 Hz), 6.68 (dd, 1H,
J = 8.0, 1.5 Hz), 6.79 (d, 1H, J = 2.8 Hz), 6.86 (d, 1H, J = 8.7 Hz),
6.94-7.04 (m, 1H), 7.07-7.17 (m, 1H), 7.42 (dd, 1H, J = 8.0, 1.5 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (in 1st stage)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design and Synthesis of Novel Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2
(HER2)/Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor (EGFR) Dual Inhibitors Bearing a
Pyrrolo[3,2-d]pyrimidine Scaffold
