$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-Bromo-7-[(3,5-di-tert-butyl)phenoxy]-2,3-dicyanonaphthalene (6). 3.36
g. of 6,7-dibromodicyanonaphthalene (5)26 (10 mmol), 2.27 g of
3,5-di-tert-butylphenol (11 mmol), and 9 g of K2CO3 (66 mmol) were mixed
together in DMF (50 mL) under argon and heated at 100 °C for 3 h (the
completion of the reaction was followed with thin-layer chromatography
using dichloromethane as solvent). The mixture was cooled till room
temperature and then stirred upon addition of 0.4 L of ice water. After 1
h of stirring the white-yellowish solid was collected and washed again
with water. The compound was dried in a vacuum at 70 °C overnight.
Recrystallization from ethanol gave 4.5 g of 6 (97%).
6-Bromo-7-[(3,5-di-tert-butyl)phenoxy]-2,3-dicyanonaphthalene (6). Yield
4.5 g (97%). MS (EI, 70 eV): 461.3 [M+], 435.3 [M+ - CN], 381.3 [M+ -
Br]. 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ): 1.30 (s, 18H, C(CH3)3), 6.66 (d, 2H, H-9), 7.38
(t, 1H, H-11), 7.69 (s, 1H, H-5), 8.40 (s, 1H, H-7), 8.61 (s, 1H, H-3),
8.79 (s, 1H, H-2). 13C NMR (CDCl3): 29.7, 29.9 (CH3), 35.3, (C-tBu),
106.0, 106.3 (C-1), 110.0 (CBr), 113.2 (CN), 115.4 (C-5), 116.0 (C- 11),
124.7, 126.0 (C-6), 127.4 (C-7), 136.0 (C-9), 138.7 (C-3), 148.4 (C-4),
151.0 (C-8), 156.0 (C-10).
