$DATUM Preparation of 5. Complex 3 (2.463 g, 3 mmol), compound 4 (0.372 g, 3
mmol) and potassium carbonate (0.553 g, 4.0 mmol) were stirred in 15mL of
DMF under a nitrogen atmosphere for 16 h at room temperature. The
solution was poured into 10% HCl and ammonium hexafluorophosphate (0.489
g, 3 mmol) was added. The precipitate was filtrated through a crucible,
dried under reduced pressure, dissolved in acetone, passed through an
alumina column and then added to water. The resulting coloured
precipitate was collected in a crucible and dried under reduced pressure.
Yield 96%. 1H NMR (acetone-d6): δ =1.30 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H, CH3), 3.75
(q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H, CH2), 4.05 (t, J = 5.1 Hz, 2H,CH2), 4.63-4.68 (m, 4H,
CH2), 5.30 (s, 5H, Cp), 6.36 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H, complexed Ar), 6.47 (d,
J = 7.4 Hz, 2H, complexed Ar), 7.10 (d, J = 9.4 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 7.27 (d, J
= 8.6 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H, Ar-H), 7.43-7.55 (m, 4H,
Ar-H), 7.88-7.98 (m, 4H, Ar-H), 8.10 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H, Ar-H). 13C NMR
(acetone-d6): δ =12.45 (CH3), 46.25, 49.37, 63.16, 63.73 (CH2), 75.68,
77.64 (complexed Ar-CH), 79.03 (Cp), 98.41 (complexed Ar-C), 113.11,
120.24, 121.08, 123.07, 124.21, 127.11 (Ar-CH), 127.82 (Ar-C), 128.16,
129.49 (Ar-CH), 129.54, 129.65 (Ar-C), 132.32 (complexed Ar-C), 132.92
(Ar-CH), 134.54, 141.66, 152.91, 154.07, 159.13, 165.76 (Ar-C), 177.87
(C=O). IR (KBr): 1725 cm-1 (C=O).
