$DATUM 127-19-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative procedure B. Copper(I) thiophene-2-carboxylate
(CuTC)-mediatedintramolecular cyclization (with workup under acidic
conditions). 2-Chloro-8-fluoro-dibenzofuran (15c). A 10 mL microwave vial
was charged with 2',5'-dichloro-5-fluoro-biphenyl-2-ol (50 mg, 0.19 mmol,
1.0 eq) and N,N-dimethylacetamide(2.0 mL). The solution was sparged with
dry nitrogen for 2 min.Copper(I) thiophene-2-carboxylate (CuTC, 48 mg,
0.25 mmol, 1.3 equiv.) was then added. The vial was sealed under a
nitrogen atmosphere and heated under microwave irradiation at 140 °C for
20 min. The reaction mixture was diluted with 0.2 M HCl (10 mL) and
extracted with dichloromethane (10 mL). The organic layer was washed with
saturated NaHCO3 solution (10 mL) and water (10 mL x 3), dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (eluent: 20-70% dichloromethane in hexanes).
2-Chloro-8-fluoro-dibenzofuran, white crystalline solid, yield 41 mg,
96%. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 7.83 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H),7.81 (dd, J =
8.6, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.45 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.37 (dd, J = 8.7, 2.2 Hz,
1H), 7.26 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.2 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (td, J = 9.0, 2.3 Hz, 1H); 13C
NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 162.7 (d, JC-F = 246.5 Hz), 157.1 (d, JC-F =
13.5 Hz), 155.1 (d, JC-F = 2.2 Hz), 128.6, 126.7, 125.1, 121.4 (d, JC-F =
10.4 Hz), 120.8, 119.6 (d, JC-F = 2.1 Hz), 112.6, 111.2 (d, JC-F = 24.0
Hz), 99.9 (d, JC-F = 26.9 Hz); MS (EI+): calculated for C12H6ClFO [M+],
220.0; m/z found, 220.1; Anal. Calculated for C12H6ClFO: C, 65.33; H,
2.74; N,0.00; found: C, 65.14; H, 2.65; N, less than 0.05.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile Assembly of Fused Benzo[4,5]furo Heterocycles
