$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-Iodo-4'-nitrodiphenyl ether (INE): To a solution of
p-iodophenol (5.05 g, 22.9 mmol) and potassium carbonate (3.73 g, 27.4
mmol) in a dehydrated DMAc (35 mL) was added p-fluoronitrobenzene (2.30
mL, 21.7 mmol) under a nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was
stirred for 24 h at room temperature, and poured into a 1 M hydrochloric
acid solution. The precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with
water and dried at 50°C in vacuo. The crude solid was purified by
recrystallization from isopropanol (IPA) and distilled water to give
product. White crystals, yield 7.17 g, 96%. IR (KBr), ν (cm-1): 1508,
1342 (NO2, stretching), 1246, 1053 (C-O-C stretching). 1H NMR (CDCl3, δ,
ppm, 25 °C): 8.21 (d, J=9.6 Hz, ArH, 2H), 7.73 (d, J=8.7 Hz, ArH, 2H),
7.03 (d, J=9.0 Hz, ArH, 2H), 6.86 (d, J=9.0 Hz, ArH, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High performance volatile polymeric memory devices based on novel
triphenylamine-based polyimides containing mono- or dual-mediated phenoxy
linkages
