$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(4-(4-nitrophenoxy)phenyl)-4,5-diphenyl-1H-imidazol (NPDI). In a 100 ml
round-bottomed two-necked flask equipped with a reflux condenser and a
magnetic stirrer bar, a mixture of 3.12 g (0.01 mol) DIP, 1.37 g (0.01
mol) p-fluoronitrobenzene, and 1.50 g (0.01 mol) potassium carbonate in
40 ml N,N-dimethylacetamide was refluxed at 110°C for 2 h. During this
time, the progress of the reaction was followed by thin layer
chromatography (TLC). The mixture was then cooled and poured into 100 ml
of water. The precipitated solid was collected by filtration, washed with
water and dried in a vacuum oven at 80°C for 12 h. Yield 96%. mp =
208-210°C. FT-IR (KBr, cm-1): 1522, 1346 (NO2), 1254 (C-O-C stretching)
and 1588 (C═N). Anal. Calcd. for C27H19N3O3: C, 74.82%; H, 4.38%; N,
9.69%. Found, C, 74.93%; H, 4.44%; N, 9.59%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
