$DATUM 2-Chloro-6-(4-methoxyphenoxy)benzaldehyde (1e). Purification of the crude
product by column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate=5:1) afforded the title product as a white solid in 95% isolated
yield. M.p. 52-54 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 3.81 (s, 3H), 6.72
(dd, J = 8.4 Hz, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 6.91-7.02 (m, 4H), 7.12 (dd, J = 7.8, 0.4
Hz, 1H), 7.32 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 10.59 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (100.6 MHz,
CDCl3, Me4Si) δ 55.5, 114.9, 115.5, 121.2, 123.3, 124.6, 134.2, 135.7,
148.5, 156.6, 161.3, 188.5. HRMS(EI) for C14H11O3Cl[M+]: calcd 262.0397,
found 262.0402.
