$DATUM Synthesis of 1-(2-p-tolyloxyphenyl)ethanone (7). (Registry Number:
103474-05-1) 1-(2-p-Tolyloxyphenyl)ethanone was prepared by the modified
literature procedure using o-bromoacetophenone (25 mmol) and p-cresol (30
mmol). The crude product was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(Rf = 0.41, EtOAc/hexane = 1/5) and distillation to give 2-(4-
methylphenoxy)acetophenone (7) (125 °C/1.0 mmHg) in 95% yield. 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 2.35 (s, 3H, CH3), 2.65 (s, 3H, CH3), 6.86-7.84 (m, 8H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 20.61, 31.54, 118.77, 119.05, 123.08, 130.22, 130.50,
130.56, 133.61, 133.64, 154.07, 157.06, 199.30; MS m/z (% relative
intensity) 226 (34), 211 (37), 119 (21), 108 (100), 105 (15), 91 (25), 77
(12), 65 (20), 51 (11); IR (neat) 3066 w, 3032 w, 2999 w, 2924 w, 2866 w,
1682 s, 1599 m, 1506 m, 1477 m, 1448 m, 1421 w, 1360 m, 1286 m, 1234 s,
1163 w, 1115 w, 1066 w, 1018 w, 966 w, 876 m, 837 w, 766 m, 596 m, 505 w,
459 w cm-1; Anal. Calcd for C15H14O2: C, 79.62; H, 6.24%. Found: C,
79.38; H, 6.06%.
