$DATUM Methyl 3-(2-Chloro-4-nitrophenoxy)benzoate (6). A mixture of
2-chloro-1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (4, 5.27 g, 30.0 mmol), methyl
3-hydroxybenzoate (5, 4.79 g, 31.5 mmol) and potassium carbonate (6.22 g,
45.0 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF) (30 mL) was stirred at room
temperature for 4 h. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo and
then, to the residue was added water (100 mL). The mixture was extracted
with ethyl acetate (EtOAc, 500 mL). The separated organic layer was
washed with brine (100 mL), dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography (eluent,
EtOAc/hexane = 1:9 to 1:4) to give 6. (9.18 g, 95%), pale yellow oil. 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 3.93 (3H, s), 6.92 (1H, d, J = 9.1 Hz), 7.28−7.34 (1H, m),
7.53 (1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.70−7.75 (1H, m), 7.92−7.98 (1H, m), 8.08 (1H,
dd, J = 9.1, 2.7 Hz), 8.41 (1H, d, J = 2.5 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design and Synthesis of Pyrrolo[3,2-d]pyrimidine Human Epidermal Growth
Factor Receptor 2 (HER2)/Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor (EGFR) Dual
Inhibitors: Exploration of Novel Back-Pocket Binders
