$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-tert-Butyl-1-(2-chloro-4-nitrophenoxy)-4-methoxybenzene (7a): A mixture
of 3-tert-butyl- 4-hydroxyanisole (3.60 g, 20 mmol),
3-chloro-4-fluoro-nitrobenzene (3.51 g, 20 mmol) and K2CO3 (3.32 g, 24
mmol) in acetonitrile (100 mL) was heated at reflux temperature during 4
hours. After cooling down, the reaction mixture was poured into water,
extracted with CH2Cl2, and the combined organic layers dried over MgSO4.
After flash column chromatography (5/5 : CH2Cl2 / heptane) 7a was
obtained. Yellow viscous oil, yield 6.4 g, 95 %. 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 8.39 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (dd, J = 9.2, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J =
2.8 Hz, 1H), 6.80 (m, 3H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 1.34 (s, 9H) ppm; 13C-NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ 160.4, 157.5, 146.8, 144.0, 142.5, 127.0, 124.5, 124.2,
123.0, 116.1, 115.0, 111.9, 56.1, 35.4, 30.7 ppm; mp 78-79 °C; HRMS calcd
for [C17H18NO4Cl] 335.0924, found 335.0914.
