$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 9-bromo-1-fluorodibenzo[b, f][1,4]oxazepin-11(10H)-one (40) Following the
general procedure II, N-(2-bromo-6-hydroxyphenyl)-2,6-difluorobenzamide
(32.7 mg, 0.1 mmol), K2CO3 (27.6 mg, 0.2 mmol) and 1.5 ml acetone were
used. The reaction mixture was stirred at 100 °C for 8h. After completion
of the reaction, the residue was purified by silical gel column
chromatography (petroleum ether: ethyl acetate = 5:1). Finally, compound
(40) was isolated. (29 mg, white solid), 95% yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm) 7.70 (s, 1H), 7.49-7.41 (m, 2H), 7.23 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H),
7.07 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.02 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm) 162.2 (d, J = 261.0 Hz), 161.1 (d, J = 3.0 Hz), 160.5, (d,
J = 4.0 Hz), 152.1, 134.13, 134.02, 130.07, 129.71, 126.54, 121.1, 116.5,
116.46, 115.04, 115.0, 114.9, 114.3, 114.1; LRMS (ESI) calcd for
C13H8BrFNO2 [M+H]+: 307.96 found 308.15
