$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of compounds I and II with phenols
III-IX in the presence of potassium carbonate in DMF (Method a) (Table
4). To a 10% solution of compound I or II in DMF we added phenol III-IX
or XVIII, and freshly calcined K2CO3, and the mixture was stirred on
heating. The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. The mixture
was cooled, the precipitate was filtered off and washed with methylene
chloride on a filter, and the filtrate was evaporated. The products
(Table 7) were isolated by chromatography on a 35 x 150-mm column charged
with Al2O3 of activity grade II (40/250 μm) using CCl4 as eluent and were
additionally purified by recrystallization. Product:
3'-Bromo-3,5'-dinitro-5-trifluoromethyldi-phenyl ether (XVI). Yield: 95%.
mp, (solvent): 70-71°C(EtOH); Formula: C13H6F3N2O5; 1H NMR spectrum, δ,
ppm (J, Hz): 7.50-7.51 m (1H, 5'-H), 7.59 m (1H, 6-H), 7.80-7.81 (1H,
4-H) , 8.00 m (1H, 2-H), 8.25-8.26 m (1H, 2'-H), 8.32 m (1H, 4-H); 19F
NMR spectrum, δP, ppm: 98.41 s (CF3); IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1540 s, 1342
s (NO2); 1231 s, 1085 m (C-O-C); 692 m (C-F); 683 m (C-Br).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Effect of the nucleophile structure on the relative mobility of the nitro
group and fluorine atom in reactions of 3,5-dinitro- and
3-fluoro-5-nitrobenzotrifluorides with phenols in the presence of
potassium carbonate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Khalfina, I. A.; Vlasov, V. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (Translation of Zhurnal
Organicheskoi Khimii) (2002), 38(1), 47-58

